# Preserve bytes exactly as committed.
#
# This is a reproducibility requirement, not a style choice. Gate reports and
# the verification manifests record sha256 digests over file CONTENT. If git
# normalises CRLF to LF on checkout, a file's bytes differ from the bytes its
# digest was computed over, and `reproduce.py` reports drift that is really
# just git rewriting the file. Disabling all text conversion keeps a clone
# byte-identical to the tree that was verified.
* -text

# Binary artifacts, marked so git never attempts a textual diff or merge.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
